\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan warns against excessive  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves as yen firm\b0\par\par\uc2 848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2010\par 03:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finmin Noda says paying utmost attention to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves\par \par \uc2 * Tokyo's warnings on yen moves unchanged from last week\par \par \uc2 * Ex-BOJ Hirano: \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely\par \par \uc2 * BOJ seen on hold but eyeing yen, may act if moves sharp (Adds comments by ex-BOJ official in paragraphs 14-15)\par \par \uc2 By Rie Ishiguro and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Japan's finance minister warned against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on Monday as expectations of U.S. easing edged the yen towards 15-year highs on the dollar, but its rise is seen as too gradual to make Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  act just yet.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities, worried a strengthening yen could harm a fragile export-led recovery and prolong deflation, have already expressed concern as the yen has neared 85 per dollar and come within sight of levels not seen since 1995.\par \par \uc2 But as long as the yen's climb is gradual, the Bank of Japan is likely to stand pat on policy at a review on Tuesday and stick to its view that the economy is on track for a moderate recovery.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has bounced back to around 85.40 yen after hitting an eight-month trough of 85.02 yen on Friday, but traders say it has room to fall again on expectations the Federal Reserve could ease monetary policy further even as early as this week. The Fed also meets on Tuesday, with a decision expected around 1815 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely watching market moves and may consider easing again if the yen nears an all-time high of 79.75 per dollar at a pace fast enough to damage business sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "With the dollar on the verge of falling below 85 yen, the BOJ will come under pressure from markets to ease further in the next few weeks," said Junko Nishioka, chief Japan economist at RBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 "It is unlikely to move at its meeting this week but may tweak the wording in its statement to include a cautious view on markets."\par \par \uc2 Global stocks and the dollar fell on Friday after disappointing U.S. payrolls data for July signalled the recovery in the world's biggest economy was losing traction.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda repeated a recent warning that disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were undesirable.\par \par \uc2 "Excessive, disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves would have adverse effects on the stability of the economy," Noda told reporters. "We will give our utmost attention to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets did not react to the remarks, which were similar to comments made by officials last week and signal Tokyo is worried about the yen, although not enough to escalate its warnings just yet, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "But the fact (Noda) has started to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves since last week shows that authorities are starting to get alarmed, and the sense of alarm may heighten in the future," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Japanese authorities' caution may intensify if the Nikkei average drops below 9,000, as share prices affect consumer and corporate sentiment."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SEEN UNLIKELY\par \par \uc2 A former senior Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters in an interview that the yen's current rise is too rapid and may prompt the Japanese authorities to step up their verbal warnings.\par \par \uc2 But Eiji Hirano, who attended Group of Seven meetings while at the BOJ, also said on Monday that Tokyo is unlikely to be able to convince the United States and Europe of the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei fell 0.7 percent on Monday to close at 9,572. It dipped close to 9,000 at the start of July but has not been below that level since May last year.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb yen gains is small, given it would have difficulty convincing its Group of Seven counterparts of the need to act at a time when its economy is recovering.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, when a 15-month yen selling spree came to an end. During that period it sold 35 trillion yen ($409.4 billion) to curb yen strength and support exporting industries.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen as difficult, the onus is likely to be on the BOJ, although with interest rates already near zero the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have many effective policy options left to support the economy.\par \par \uc2 The economy likely slowed considerably in the April-June quarter after expanding an annualised 5 percent in the first quarter, a Reuters poll showed, as export growth moderated and a boost to consumer spending from government incentives faded.\par \par \uc2 In a sign the abundant cash pumped out by the BOJ is not reaching broad sectors of the economy, bank lending fell 1.8 percent in July from a year earlier to mark the eighth straight month of declines. ($1=85.49 Yen) (Editing by Charlotte Cooper and Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|Table|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100809e6890001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
