\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-Ex-BOJ Taya: BOJ may ease if dlr below 80 yen\b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2010\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Japan policymakers on edge over rising yen\par \par \uc2 * Dollar falling broadly due to worries about U.S. economy\par \par \uc2 * BOJ to meet on Aug. 9-10, policy move not ruled out (Adds details, direct quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White and Shigeo Kodama\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan could ease policy further should the dollar break below 80 yen by extending the size or duration of a fixed interest rate funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Teizo Taya, a former BOJ board member, said on Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the dollar moves 3 to 4 yen in one day, Taya told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Speculation has intensified over whether authorities may consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might relax its already ultra-loose monetary policy to curb the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 Policy-makers are worried that the yen's strength could undermine Japanese exports, which have led the economy out of the global downturn, and add to deflationary pressures following 16 straight months of falling consumer prices.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2004 and some economists say it would be hard to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time when other Group of Seven countries are pushing for China to allow the yuan to rise.\par \par \uc2 Since Japan's government can do little to stop the rising yen beyond actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pressure is likely to fall on the BOJ to take some measures to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gain.\par \par \uc2 "Exports are already slowing, so if the yen rises further, production slows and corporate earnings fall, then it's possible the BOJ could to ease further," he said.\par \par \uc2 "For the BOJ, the level of dollar/yen would be important. If dollar/yen breaks 80 there would be a lot of complaints from businesses and the BOJ might respond. The BOJ might expand the amount of the fixed-interest rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The duration could be expanded to six months, or maybe even one year to have more impact." <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ BOJ eyes yen before Aug. 10 policy meeting [ID:nTOE67405T] Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise? [ID:nTOE672023] More stories on the Japanese economy [ID:nECONJP] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded at 86.08 yen <JPY=> on Friday, up 0.3 percent on the day and more than 1 yen above its November low of 84.82 yen, a break of which would take it to a 15-year low.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ is unlikely to change policy at a two-day policy meeting ending on Aug. 10. But there is a possibility the BOJ could take minor steps if the yen shoots up.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe a BOJ decision, under government pressure, to set up a fixed-rate bank funding scheme in December was designed to help cool the yen, suggesting further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action could be considered.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, when their 15-month yen selling spree came to an end. During that period, they sold 35 trillion yen ($408 billion) to curb the yen's strength and support the country's exporting industries.\par \par \uc2 Taya, who left the BOJ board in 2004 after serving for five years, is currently an adviser at the \uc2 Daiwa Institute of Research\uc2  in Tokyo. (Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100809e686000jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
