\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Vietnam Shares Down 0.1% On Credit Supply Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 1,695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2010\par 05:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0329 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares last down 0.1% at 486.05 after touching 489.2 earlier with some investors selling amid rising concerns \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will act slowly in boosting cash flows into the economy, and hopes for a quick increase of credit supply are waning. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has already fixed its benchmark rate at 8% for this month, and if it wants to ease borrowing costs for companies, we will have to wait for September, and weak inflows will certainly pull down share prices in the coming days," says trader. Volume thin with 23 million shares valued at VND700 billion traded. Among decliners, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam Finance\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PVF.VH) down 2.2% at VND22,300, Masan (MSN.VH) down 1.0% at VND52,000, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hoang Anh Gia Lai (HAG.VH) \f28 \uc2 \f2 down 0.6% at VND78,500. Tips immediate support at 485. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0329 GMT [Dow Jones] RBNZ may pause current rate hike cycle as early as September, according to snap poll of 13 economists after today's weaker-than-expected 2Q labor data; economists now see 60% chance of rate hike, 40% chance of pause; in previous poll all economists tipped September rate hike. While September pause may be on cards, majority still expecting pause in October with two tipping December, while \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  reiterates no pause expected this year. Previously four had said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep hiking for next three meetings at least. "Today's report combined with the weaker commodity price news of late clearly favours our view that the next policy review on September 16 will likely see the last rate hike for this year," says Darren Gibbs, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  Chief Economist. Adds "with even that hike likely to be called into question if economic and other developments continue to disappoint in coming weeks." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0326 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares last +0.4% at 870.62 in active trade. Upside likely limited as upward GDP revision largely priced in; buying in big caps subsides after benchmark up 16% since end May on back of strengthening economy, says Far East Securities analyst Weerachai Krongsamsri. Adds profit taking expected to cap SET Index at 875, but support at 860 should hold as overall sentiment remains positive. Among top actives, \uc2 Sri Trang Agro Industry\uc2  (STA.TH) +4.2% at THB22.50, Thai Rubber Latex Corporation (TRUBB.TH) +6.7% at THB9.60, \uc2 True Corporation\uc2  (TRUE.TH) +5.9% at THB5.40, \uc2 Charoen Pokphand Foods\uc2  (CPF.TH) +1.3% at THB24.10, TMB Bank (TMB.TH) flat at THB2.12. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0317 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex called to open about 25-45 points higher, tracking positive trade in most Asian markets and as undertone remains upbeat on sustained foreign inflows, good monsoon rains recently, says dealer at local brokerage. Adds, ample liquidity, announcement from index heavyweight \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) it's forming shale gas JV with U.S. firm \uc2 Carrizo Oil & Gas\uc2  to further support. Foreign funds have bought shares worth over INR21.7 billion this month, were buyers of about INR103.6 billion in July. Still, dealer reckons Sensex to find strong resistance at 18,320 for session, as valuations stretched in most index stocks after over 9.6% rally since June 9. Adds, outperformance last 3 months vs most emerging markets could also lead to som