ighlight\uc2  appreciation given the likelihood that the RBI would step in to absorb the inflows." Adds, while INR looks set to rise near term, house expects it to decline, with USD/INR at 47 in 3 months, 47.5 in 6 months; keeps 12 month forecast at 46.5. Pair at 46.18 late Wednesday. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0247 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei up 1.3% at 9609.30 midday on U.S. stocks' gains and weaker yen, but intraday 9688.87 peak thus far likely to be high for day due to lack of further buying catalysts, traders say. "Short-covering was done in the morning. For the rest of the day, investors may stay sidelined," Japanese brokerage manager says, putting Nikkei resistance at 9700. Also says volume may stay low (TSE 1st section volume just 739 million shares) as investors remain concerned about U.S. economy before jobs data is out on Friday, they may not want to take large positions before then. After relatively quick start after 1Q earnings reports Toyota (7203.TO) now up just 1.1% at Y3,125, while Isuzu (7202.TO) up 6.8% at Y266; Honda (7267.TO) also up 2.1% at Y2,838. Higher USD/JPY (now 86.17) helping major tech exporters such as Fanuc (6954.TO), up 2.7% at Y10,280. Real estate leading sectoral gainer, with \uc2 Mitsui Fudosan\uc2  (8801.TO) up 3.1% at Y1,307. \uc2 Renesas Electronics\uc2  (6723.TO) off 5.2% to Y691 after \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  cuts rating to Neutral. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0248 GMT [Dow Jones] The Philippines' stable July inflation data of 3.9% gives \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility to keep rates steady. But \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  economist Prakriti Sofat says "there's a need for some policy normalization to ensure that low inflation expectations become entrenched." She adds, "with the policy rate unchanged since July 2009, the real policy rate has come down sharply-currently running well below past averages." Adds, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to begin a rate hike in 4Q with 25 bps and another hike in 2Q next year. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0242 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares up 0.9% at 3009.602, as investors buying back most bank, consumer-, commodity-related stocks after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left key interest rate unchanged at 6.5% yesterday, traders say; tip resistance at 3020. "Buying is occurring across the board, but may be short-lived due to concerns over fresh weakness in the rupiah," says trader at First Asia Capital. Among gainers, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) +1.6% at IDR9,350, car maker Astra (ASII.JK) +2.3% at IDR47,550, while tin miner Timah (TINS.JK) up 3.2% at IDR2,425. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) [ 08-04-10 2329ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100805e6850002o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
