\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Yen close to peaking against dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 853 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2010\par 14:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Full data <FOREXPOLL01>\par \par \uc2 * Weakness in the yen seen as overall trend\par \par \uc2 * One in three expect BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Shivani Singh\par \par \uc2 BANGALORE, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen, now trading near 15-year highs against the dollar, is close to peaking but its slide will be at a slightly slower pace than previously expected as recent gloomy U.S. data and prospects for extended low U.S. interest rates keep pressure on the greenback.\par \par \uc2 A monthly Reuters poll of around 60 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists taken Aug. 2-4 saw them scale back their forecasts for the dollar/yen. They saw dollar/yen trading at 86.8 in a month from now, 92 in six months and 97 in a year, compared with 89, 95 and 98 last month.\par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> is currently trading at around 85.50 per dollar, not far off a 15-year high. That has raised alarm among policymakers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength will weaken Japanese exports and add to deflationary pressures. [ID:nSGE673042]\par \par \uc2 In the short term, cracks seem to be emerging in the U.S. recovery with weaker-than-expected housing and GDP data prompting selling of the U.S. dollar and allowing the yen to regain some of its safe-haven appeal among investors.\par \par \uc2 "The yen should remain firm for the time being, as long as uncertainty over the strength of the U.S. recovery persists," said Roberto Mialich, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  MIB.\par \par \uc2 The yen's steep ascent had caught many unaware in the July poll, with only eight of 61 strategists expecting the dollar/yen to trade at or below 85 yen over the next twelve months. This number has more than doubled to 18 of 61 strategists in the latest poll.\par \par \uc2 In the last 20 Reuters polls, not once was the median prediction across the forecast horizon close to the strong 85 levels that the yen is currently trading near.\par \par \uc2 However, many say that the yen's rise is short-lived as even if the U.S. Federal Reserve waits longer before raising rates, it will still do so before the Bank of Japan (BOJ). [ECILT/US]\par \par \uc2 "USD/JPY is likely to be choppy on risk on/off shifts in the next few quarters, before entering a steady upward trend from mid-2011 on expectations of eventual Fed tightening," said Mengxian Jiao of Bank of America-Merrill Lynch.\par \par \uc2 IMPENDING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under growing pressure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's rapid rise and support Japanese exports.\par \par \uc2 One in three strategists polled said they expect the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, with about half of those expecting it as dollar/yen hits 85.\par \par \uc2 "Look for BOJ and government rhetoric to be stepped up if U.S. dollar weakness persists through 85.50, with potential discussion about additional BOJ policy stimulus and MoF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not ruled out," said Kenneth Broux, economist at Lloyds TSB Corp Markets.\par \par \uc2 "A return of safe-haven flows from equities would boost JPY demand and add downside pressure to USD/JPY in the short term," Broux added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since a 15-month period up to March 2004 when authorities sold 35 trillion yen ($408 billion) to curb the yen's strength and support the country's export industries.\par \par \uc2 The euro has lost around 14 percent to the Japanese yen <EURJPY=> so far this year as the European debt crisis rumbled on. However, cross rates calculated by Reuters show the yen gradually depreciating against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Those cross rates saw the euro trade at 113.3 yen in a month, 113.4 in six months, and 116.1 in a year compared with the 110, 111 and 115 yen respectively seen in last month's survey.\par \par \uc2 Yen volatility was seen at an annualised rate of 9.9 percent up from the 9.7 percent actual volatility last month. [VOL/POLL]\par \par \uc2 SWISSIE TO RISE AGAINST EURO\par \par \uc2 The poll expects the Swiss franc to strengthen against the euro over the 12-month forecast horizon, according to the survey's calculated cross rates <EURCHF>.\par \par \uc2 Median estimates saw the franc at 1.36 per euro in a month, strengthening to 1.33 in six months and falling back slightly to 1.35 in a year. Those forecasts compared with 1.34, 1.33 and 1.35 in the July poll.\par \par \uc2 "The current strength of the euro versus the Swiss franc should be short-lived. Higher money market rates in the euro zone as the ECB adjusts liquidity leave the euro with the upper hand versus the Swiss franc," Niels Christensen at Nordea said.\par \par \uc2 He sees more momentum in the Swiss economy compared to the euro zone, which should see the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  tigthen its monetary policy sooner and faster than the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the poll click on [ID:nLDE6721F3]) (Additional reporting by Anooja Debnath) (Polling by Bangalore Polling Unit)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YEN/POLL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|UKI|NAT|J|U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100807e6840007m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184