\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Bank Of Japan Unlikely To Intercept Rallying Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Curren   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 21:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The yen's been racing higher against the dollar like a finely tuned sports car lately, but the Bank of Japan isn't likely to set off in hot pursuit.\par \par \uc2 Instead, it seems much likelier that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stay on the sidelines and abstain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, at least in the near term.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reached levels that invite speculation about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, the dollar reached Y85.67, its worst level since it hit a 15-year low at Y84.82 in November 2009. Because yen strength reduces demand for the country's export products, the Japanese government has taken action in the past to quell the yen's advance.\par \par \uc2 Direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the most effective tool for reducing any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -induced damage to Japan's struggling economy available to ministers at the finance department, who make the decisions about market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are executed by the bank.\par \par \uc2 But market watchers believe the most recent signals from Japanese officials suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a low probability event.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister Yoshihiko Noda said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in principle should be set by market forces, although he added that disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements could hurt economic activities.\par \par \uc2 "Regarding how to respond to (recent yen rises), our fundamental stance is that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are something that should basically be set by the market," Noda said during a session of the Lower House's fiscal and financial committee.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains out of favor with the world's leading central banks. The Group of Seven leading nations has shunned \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for many years and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been active in markets to slow the yen's climb since 2004.\par \par \uc2 "I think the bar for BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be high," said Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Conditions in the market don't line up with those typically associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 The options market is not showing a one-way trade in the dollar against the yen, with a big premium on yen calls over yen puts, he said. While the BOJ typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times of high volatility, volatility is at the low end of its ranges for the last few months, Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 Beyond that, the yen's appreciation is not just a yen move, but reflects broadly based weakness in the dollar, he said.\par \par \uc2 In a report in early July, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said its proprietary model for yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was then estimating a 47% probability of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That was up from 40% at the end of May and extended an uptrend that began in late 2009.\par \par \uc2 The traditional indicators of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have risen since then, but political changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  tend to work against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Ron Leven, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Party of Japan, which took over as the ruling party last year, appears less oriented to a weak yen than its predecessor, the Liberal Democratic Party, he said.\par \par \uc2 A power vacuum in Japan, where the DPJ lost its majority in the upper house last month, also militates against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 "In the very short term, it makes it difficult to get the organization and focus together that's needed to do a serious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Leven said.\par \par \uc2 (Don Curren, a reporter based in Toronto, has covered Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income markets for more than 10 years. He can be reached at 416-306-2020 or at don.curren@dowjones.com.)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments [ 08-03-10 1536ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100803e683000ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
