\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Q+A-Will  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene \highlight\uc2  to curb yen's rise?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Masayuki Kitano and Hideyuki Sano    \par \uc2 1,093 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 03:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  (Repeats item that first ran late on Monday)\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 2 (Reuters) - A broad fall in the dollar has propelled the yen higher, bringing the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within range of levels it has not traded at for 15 years and raising speculation whether even more gains will tempt Japanese authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an eight-month low of 85.95 yen last week, having shed about 6 percent since mid-June as weak economic data sparked worries about the sustainability of a U.S. recovery. \par \par \uc2  A further drop in the dollar below a trough set last November at 84.82 yen would take the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a 15-year peak and bring it ever closer to its 1995 record high of 79.75 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  The yen stood near 86.70 yen to the dollar <JPY=> on Monday, off last week's high but still stuck at levels that could hurt Japanese exporters.\par \par \uc2  WHAT WOULD HEIGHTEN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers won't seriously expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar drops below November's low of 84.82 yen.\par \par \uc2  The yen's rise would have to speed up and a fall in Japanese shares would have to deepen for authorities to get really concerned, market players say.\par \par \uc2  But the yen has hardly been volatile. Its one-month historical volatility is around 12 percent, below the past five years' average of 13.7 percent and way below a peak above 30 percent in late 2008.\par \par \uc2  Thus Japan may have a hard time convincing other G7 partners about the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just when they are calling on China to make its yuan more flexible to ease global imbalances.\par \par \uc2  Any attempt to cheapen the yen could run counter to U.S. President Barack Obama's plan to double U.S. exports, raising diplomatic obstacles to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  To be sure, the yen's rise has helped make Japan's benchmark Nikkei share average <.N225> one of the worst performers in the region in the past month. But the average has managed to stay above a trough hit in November when the yen last surged.\par \par \uc2  Seasoned \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders also say the market is not gripped with the nervous tension which accompanies \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations.\par \par \uc2  For instance, option markets are not pricing in a jump in yen volatility -- an unusual development when the yen is so close to historic peaks. One-month implied volatility <JPY1MO=> is about 11 percent, near a 2-1/2-month low of about 10 percent last week.   <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   For graphics:\par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen spot rate and 1-month implied volatility\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/hep72n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/hep72n}}}\par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen spot rate and yen's effective exchange rate\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/hyq68m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/hyq68m}}}\uc2   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2  HAS \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  ABANDONED ITS OLD \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONIST\b0 \highlight\uc2  WAYS?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2004, when a 15-month long yen selling spree came to an end.\par \par \uc2  During that period, they sold 35 trillion yen ($400 billion), the equivalent of more than a third of the annual budget, to try to stop a rising yen from harming all-important exports and to fight deflation.\par \par \uc2  Even a rare G7 statement between meetings in October 2008, which singled out yen volatility and was seen as giving \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  approval to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , did not tempt Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  Many analysts think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a drop in the ocean when the yen is rising against a broadly weakening dollar. In fact, the score card for the 2003-2004 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mixed at best as the yen continued to gain gradually during the campaign.\par \par \uc2  Fear of losses could also make Tokyo reluctant after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to curb strength in the Swiss franc, faced criticism at home when it suffered losses of over 14 billion francs ($13.5 billion) from its franc selling.\par \par \uc2  In March, Japan's then-Finance Minister, Naoto Kan, said in parliament its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account already had net paper loss of around 5 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2  SO IS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  OUT OF THE QUESTION?\par \par \uc2  To rein in the yen's rise, the authorities did check market rates with commercial banks last November for possible dollar buying, though they stopped short of making orders, a tactic known as rate-checking. They are seen as likely to employ this again should the yen rise further.\par \par \uc2  But many market players expect Tokyo's efforts to thwart yen gains are likely to focus more on monetary policy.\par \par \uc2  Under government pressure, the BOJ also called an emergency meeting in early December and decided to pump 10 trillion yen in three-month funds into the banking system, a move many market sources said was aimed at the yen more than anything.\par \par \uc2  Some market players speculate the BOJ could offer cheap funds to banks for six months, rather than the current three months, if the yen threatens to rise further.\par \par \uc2  Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Citibank \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tended to happen when the yen's real effective exchange rate has risen around or above two standard deviations above its five-year moving average.\par \par \uc2  The yen's effective rate would hit that level if the dollar falls below 85 yen and stays there consistently.\par \par \uc2  Outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible if the dollar breaks below its November trough and nears the 1995 record low, said Tomoko Fujii, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  WHAT HAVE OFFICIALS SAID?\par \par \uc2  So far their comments have been pretty low-key.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and the BOJ conducts any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf.\par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Monday: "Excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves are undesirable because of the impact they have on the economy and financial markets. From that standpoint, we are watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves closely." [ID:nTOE67001Q]\par \par \uc2  His deputy, Motohisa Ikeda, is known to have favoured a weaker yen but since he took the post in June, he has avoided strong comments, saying in general he is worried about the impact of the yen's rise on the export industry. [ID:nTFD006498]\par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa has said the yen's rise and stock price falls may affect the economy, but has stuck to the view the economy is on a recovery trend. [ID:nTFD006502]  ($1=1.041 Swiss Franc)  ($1=86.45 Yen)  (Editing by Charlotte Cooper)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Q+A, REPEAT)|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100803e6830005z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
