\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  may be a losing game\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tamawa Desai  \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2010\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 30 (Reuters) - The adverse effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a recent foray by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) shows, may deter governments in major economies from entering into an increasingly losing game.\par \par \uc2 The yen's recent strength, partly on the back of a weaker dollar stemming from concerns about the U.S. economy, has renewed speculation Japanese authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen.\par \par \uc2 But, with daily volume of some $3 trillion, some participants say the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is too large for authorities to control the levels of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Recent cases have also shown market volatility actually rises after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The SNB used unprecendented amounts to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and at best only slowed the pace of (Swiss franc) appreciation, but it increased volatility," said Derek Halpenny, European head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 "That is what makes it a difficult proposition for some countries like Japan, which seeks orderly moves."\par \par \uc2 When the SNB in June ended its 15-month-old policy of holding down the Swiss franc against the euro, the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high of 1.3070 francs two weeks later. It was trading around 1.3540 on Friday <CHF=>.\par \par \uc2 "Given the nature of the market, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can later on cause sharp swings in the opposite direction (to) what was intended," one senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 SNB Chairman \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  has also come under fire for losses of some 14 billion Swiss francs on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's books from its franc-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some say that would make it more difficult to justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  going forward.\par \par \uc2 Simon Derrick, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Bank of New York Mellon in London, said the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not a great experience" and it would probably take a different approach in the future.\par \par \uc2 "People were buying into the Swiss franc as a safe haven, and the SNB gave them the opportunity to buy at artificially cheaper levels," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators still held net long positions in the Swiss franc in the week ended July 20, Commodity Futures Trading Commission data showed.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo may take heed of such issues surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given its limited success in the past.\par \par \uc2 In any case, market participants do not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the dollar drops to an all-time low below 80 yen <JPY=>.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would find it extremely difficult politically to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when global pressure is on China to free up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One-month risk reversals <JPY1MRR=ICAP> also show a softer bias toward a higher yen and are nowhere near levels that would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , option traders say.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent 35 trillion yen in a 15-month period that ended in March 2004. It has since refrained from overt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even as the yen hit a 14-year high of 84.82 yen last November.\par \par \uc2 Other major monetary authorities also seem wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The United States and Britain have refrained from seeking specific levels in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a policy tool, while the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's only public foray in the euro's 11-year history was in 2000, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with its Group of Seven partners to prop up the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100730e67u001qi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
