\par\par \b \uc2 Japan stays out of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in July as yen rises vs dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2010\par 13:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 30 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from June 29 to July 28, when the yen touched its highest level against the dollar since December.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have stayed out of the market for more than six years. The last time they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen was in March 2004, when they conducted yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On July 16, the dollar fell to 86.27 yen on trading platform EBS, the lowest since early December. The dollar has since extended its losses, touching an eight-month low of 86.15 yen on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A fall below 84.82 yen on EBS would take the dollar to its lowest level against the yen in 15 years. (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|NAT|J|SI|RBN|UKI|AUF|ND|ABN|M|E|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100730e67u001jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
