\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Japan Increasingly Wary Of Strong JPY -BarCap\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2010\par 06:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0425 GMT [Dow Jones] Recent comments from Japanese politicians regarding negative impact of recently strong JPY on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy "suggest the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are rising," says Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in Japan. While Japanese government hasn't stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to tame JPY strength since 2004, says chances would increase, especially if USD/JPY falls toward 85.00, dragging down Japan share markets. Cites comments last week from trade minister Naoshima, economic, fiscal policy minister Arai that stronger JPY could hurt Japanese economy; remark from parliamentary secretary Tsumura that current JPY level is little too high. Says while BOJ seems more hesitant to try to fight JPY strength with additional monetary easing, BOJ/government divide would likely not deter government from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if JPY strengthens further. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has authority for deciding on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  USD/JPY last 87.63.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-07-10 0425GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100726e67q0009e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal