\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls vs yen as risk cut after Bernanke\b0\par\par\uc2 1,071 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2010\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Dollar/yen falls as risk appetite wanes following Bernanke\par \par \uc2 * Fall in U.S. bond yields seen hurting greenback\par \par \uc2 * Euro/dollar stalls ahead of Europe's stress tests\par \par \uc2 * Wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hampers yen\par \par \uc2 By Hideyuki Sano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 22 (Reuters) - The dollar slid towards a recent seven-month low versus the yen on Thursday after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke expressed concern about the U.S. economy but steered clear of hinting about further easing as some had hoped.\par \par \uc2 The euro, which lost sharply after his comments sparked outflows from stocks and other risk assets, held steady at lower levels ahead of Europe's bank stress test results on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Bernanke, in testimony prepared for delivery to the Senate Banking Committee, said the U.S. economy faces "unusually uncertain" prospects. [ID:nN21165172]\par \par \uc2 "That 'unusually uncertain' phrase from Bernanke was very strong, prompting investors to sell stocks and buy government bonds," said a trader at a big Japanese bank.\par \par \uc2 "But in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, investors are unable to react much before the stress test results, the market's main focus."\par \par \uc2 Although Bernanke said the Fed was ready to take further steps to bolster growth if needed, analysts said lack of clarity on what measures it could take prompted investors to reduce risk positions, benefiting the low-yielding yen across the board.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.7 percent to 86.47 yen <JPY=>, extending losses after a 0.5 percentage point fall on Wednesday, on a mixture of offers from Japanese exporters and hedging selling related to some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked structured notes.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar could fall fast if it breaks below a seven-month trough of 86.27 yen hit last week, with stop-loss dollar offers believed to be waiting below that level.\par \par \uc2 A relentless drop in U.S. bond yields is also reducing the allure of the dollar in comparison with the yen.\par \par \uc2 The two-year U.S. Treasury note yield fell to a record low around 0.56 percent following Bernanke's comments, shrinking the yield spread of two-year U.S bonds over Japanese government debt to a fresh 15-month low.\par \par \uc2 Others were less convinced about the likelihood of further falls in the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The pair's 14-day relative strength index is at 33, near the 30 mark considered to indicate an oversold market.\par \par \uc2 Yuki Sakasai, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 , said the dollar/yen rate was unlikely to fall much below the seven-month low for now.\par \par \uc2 "What Bernanke has said is essentially the same as the minutes (of the Fed's June 22-23 meeting). So his comments alone are unlikely to push the dollar/yen below recent trading ranges," Sakasai said.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the yen, which gained steeply on the crosses on Wednesday, has been hampered by caution that Japanese policy makers may try to talk it down as it nears a 14-year high around 85 yen per dollar hit last November.\par \par \uc2 Deputy Finance Minister Motohisa Ikeda said on Thursday Japan wants to avoid excessive rises in the yen, but market reaction was muted. [ID:nTOE66L012]\par \par \uc2 The euro was up 0.2 percent at $1.2781 <EUR=>, winning some reprieve after having lost nearly 1 percent on Wednesday on Bernanke's comments and tepid demand at a Portuguese debt sale.\par \par \uc2 It has some support at its 14-day moving average around $1.2742 and around $1.2720, a July 9 high.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to consolidate around the current levels, as few traders will be eager to push it higher before the European Union unveils the stress tests on euro zone banks.\par \par \uc2 The euro has had a good run against the dollar in recent weeks, rising to a 10-week high above $1.30 on Tuesday as traders began to bet most of the 91 European banks being examined would pass the tests. [ID:nLDE66K0YO]\par \par \uc2 European policy makers have expressed confidence their banks will pass, although some analysts say investors remain sceptical about the severity of the checks.\par \par \uc2 Major listed banks, which face constant investor scrutiny, are expected to pass, but the tests may show the worst problems lie with smaller players such as Spanish cajas and German landesbanks, which are mainly unlisted. [ID:nLDE66J0GP]\par \par \uc2 Euro/dollar 1-month risk reversal <EUR1MRR=ICAP>, a measure of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment, showed a slight bias for euro puts.\par \par \uc2 Traders said that was partly reflecting some fears among players that the euro may start falling after the euro zone bank stress test results.\par \par \uc2 Data from broker ICAP <EURVOL=ICAP> shows euro/dlr 1-mth risk reversal standing at 1.25/1.75%, its highest since early July.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rika Otsuka; Editing by Michael Watson) ((hideyuki.sano@thomsonreuters.com; +81 3 6441 1827; Reuters Messaging: hideyuki.sano.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 All data taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 2130 GMT in the previous New York session.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Last  US Close    Pct   YTD Pct   2009\par                                      Change  Change    Close\par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr   <EUR=>      1.