\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro dips, pulls away from 2-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2010\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Euro cedes ground as rally pauses, Hungary weighs\par \par \uc2 * Yen hovers near 7-mth highs vs USD\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 19 (Reuters) - The euro pulled back from two-month highs on Monday, as investors booked profits on its rally while lingering concerns about Europe's sovereign debt problems looked likely to keep a lid on future gains.\par \par \uc2 High-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Australian and New Zealand dollars were also under pressure as subdued U.S. data and falling equities <.SPX> led investors to shun risky trades.\par \par \uc2 Trade was light in Asia with Tokyo shut for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 The euro <EUR=> dipped 0.2 percent to $1.2904, pulling back from a two-month high of $1.3008 hit on Friday on trading platform EBS, with news that the International Monetary Fund and the European Union have suspended a review of Hungary's funding programme putting some pressure on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This means Hungary will not have access to remaining funds in its $25.1 bln package. [ID:nLDE66H021]. Dealers said this reminded investors of the region's sovereign debt problems just days ahead of the results of stress tests on euro zone's banks. The results are due out of Friday.\par \par \uc2 "While European leaders believe that the tests will bring confidence, the markets may not believe the sugar-coated figures with the euro primed for another leg down in the weeks ahead," said David Scutt, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Arab Bank, Australia.\par \par \uc2 "Heavy selling pressure is expected to emerge ahead of resistance at $1.3100-10."\par \par \uc2 Near term support for the euro is seen around the $1.2850 area, the 50 percent retracement of the euro's fall from a high near $1.3820 on March 17 to a four-year low of $1.1876 hit in early June. Traders said there was talk of light stops around $1.2880.\par \par \uc2 The dollar edged up 0.1 percent against the yen to 86.64 yen <JPY=> but was not far from a seven-month low of 86.27 yen hit on Friday on EBS.\par \par \uc2 Latest data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission showed speculators have been increasing long positions in the yen and cutting longs in the U.S. dollar. <IMM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 >.\par \par \uc2 EYES ON YEN\par \par \uc2 Traders said with U.S. yields heading lower, the dollar could break past support near its seven-month low.\par \par \uc2 Such a drop could spark speculation of potential Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the yen, especially if the dollar drops to a 15-year low by breaching the November 2009 trough of 84.82 on EBS.\par \par \uc2 With the yen's latest rise having brought it to levels that could cause pain to Japanese exporters, a focal point is whether Japanese authorities will take steps to curb the yen's rise, through measures such as verbal or actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or additional monetary easing measures.\par \par \uc2 "We're getting into the territory where the MOF will start to get a little bit more vociferous," said Gareth Berry, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Berry said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) may start to express concern over the exchange rate, adding that such rhetoric could help limit the dollar's downside.\par \par \uc2 "I think there is plenty of scope for further downside beyond 85 before we actually see an actual act of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not conducted any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than six years, having last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March 2004.\par \par \uc2 When the dollar slid to the 84.82 yen trough against the yen in late November, the BOJ stepped closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than at any time in the preceding five years by checking exchange rates with commercial banks. [ID:nT35213]\par \par \uc2 Soon after, the BOJ called an emergency meeting in early December and decided to pump 10 trillion yen ($115.5 billion) in three-month funds into the banking system.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, a private survey showed U.S. consumer sentiment weakened in early July to an 11-month low and capped a week which saw U.S. data printing on the softer side, raising questions about the sustainability of a U.S. recovery. [ID:nN15208925].\par \par \uc2 A resulting slide in U.S. stocks <.SPX> hit growth-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Australian dollar, which dipped 0.2 percent to $0.8680 <AUD=D4>. Earlier, traders said a model fund was seen selling the Aussie, which shed 1.6 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Anirban Nag and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Krishna Kumar in Sydney; editing by Kazunori Takada)\par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|GNN|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100719e67j000ab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
