\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Hits 2-Mo Low Vs Yen On US Econ Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2010\par 07:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell to a two-month low against the yen in Asia Thursday, as recent weak U.S. data increased concerns about that nation's economy, propelling large Japanese investors to aggressively sell the unit.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session, the greenback briefly dropped to Y88.08, its lowest level since May 6. Tokyo dealers said it will likely keep falling this week.\par \par \uc2 "I see plenty of dollar-selling offers from various types of large Japanese players ranging from exporters to banks to funds," said a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank said.\par \par \uc2 Exporters were in a particular hurry, he said, probably because the exchange rate is below their break-even point.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's tankan survey of firms released earlier in the day showed that firms made business plans for this fiscal year ending in March on the assumption the greenback will trade at Y90.18 on average. If the yen rises further, earnings generated overseas could shrink significantly when repatriated.\par \par \uc2 As of 0450 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at Y88.26 from Y88.43 in New York Wednesday. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 86.140 from 86.031.\par \par \uc2 The dollar may soon slip below the psychologically important Y88.00 mark and head toward Y85.00 if the Institute for Supply Management's manufacturing index due at 1400 GMT misses forecasts. Dealers said a weaker-than-expected reading will push shares and U.S. Treasury yields down, which would in turn increase demand for the safe-haven yen.\par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones poll of economists forecasts the headline figure for the data to deteriorate to 59.0 in June from 59.7 in May.\par \par \uc2 Even if the greenback falls to Y85.00, the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is low because the economy is no longer so weak as to justify such action, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "As economic conditions improve and exporters become tougher, it's getting difficult for the MOF to take any actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citi Bank Japan.\par \par \uc2 The euro, meanwhile, was at Y107.80 and $1.2214 from Y108.21 and $1.2238 New York Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The euro's outlook is also grim because of ongoing spontaneous global share-price declines, said \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's senior dealer Shinichi Hayashi.\par \par \uc2 He said that if the Nikkei Stock Average falls below the psychological level of 9,000, euro-selling will intensify, taking along other high-yielding but risky \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars.\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven Swiss franc should strengthen on the other hand, he said. The franc recorded another fresh all-time high against the euro, with the euro falling to CHF1.3073 earlier in the day. Dealers said the euro should soon drop below CHF1.30.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Lo