\par\par \b \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS 3-BOJ's Shirakawa hints may do more to help economy\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2010\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 21 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa signalled on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider further steps besides a new loan programme in trying to boost the country's potential economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Following are key quotes from Shirakawa's news conference:\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL MARKET MOVES\par \par \uc2 "Japan's money market and markets for commercial paper and corporate bonds are stable compared to European and U.S. markets ...\par \par \uc2 "It may take time for some European countries to regain market confidence on fiscal conditions. During this process, we will closely examine how the global financial markets and economy will be affected.\par \par \uc2 "Recent market moves are somewhat rapid.\par \par \uc2 "Financial conditions in Japan continue to show signs of easing while some severity remains. Corporate funding costs are lowering as term interest rates are moving stably at low levels. Many small firms say their funding conditions remain severe, but overall the situation is easing."\par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN DEBT WOES\par \par \uc2 "We need to watch for downside risks for the European economy if financial market tensions heighten due to some European countries' fiscal reforms.\par \par \uc2 "But we maintain the view that emerging economies will lead the global economy's recovery and that emerging economies will maintain strong growth based on domestic demand and the United States will continue to recover moderately.\par \par \uc2 "The European economy is likely to have limited impacts on the Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 "I won't comment on the substance of G7 and other international meetings. But various international meetings including teleconferences have taken place since the weekend before last. We are keeping in close contact with each other in exchanging opinions ...\par \par \uc2 "We have agreed to continue working together to stabilise financial systems and support economic recovery."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Asked about the euro's rebound on caution and speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the possibility of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 :)\par \par \uc2 "It is not appropriate to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other countries, and if the question is about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  I won't comment as that is a matter under the jurisdiction of the finance minister."\par \par \uc2 JAPAN ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy is moving in line with the (BOJ) outlook report issued last month. The economy is starting to recover moderately on the back of improvements in overseas economies ...\par \par \uc2 "Domestic private-sector demand shows signs of a self-sustaining recovery. GDP data for January-March showed a recovery led by exports and consumption, and that underlined our view."\par \par \uc2 NEW LOAN SCHEME\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ plans to design a system for supporting a broad range of companies in various sectors. It is taking into account growth strategies presented by the government and industry groups.\par \par \uc2 "The scheme will not be a permanent measure. The BOJ plans to set a deadline.\par \par \uc2 "As it will take time for the scheme to have effects on growth, we need to take our time in supporting banks' efforts.\par \par \uc2 "We want to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in how resources are distributed to specific industries and companies.\par \par \uc2 "We have yet to set the conditions that financial institutions need to meet for the new loans ...\par \par \uc2 "The scheme doesn't mean we have changed the way we adjust money."\par \par \uc2 POSSIBLE SUPPORT FOR SECURITISED PRODUCTS\par \par \uc2 "If financial institutions were to securitise their loans for supporting economic growth, the BOJ would like to proactively participate in developing the market for such products.\par \par \uc2 "It is also worth considering an idea of accepting such securitised products as collateral in money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Rie Ishiguro; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/SHIRAKAWA (HIGHLIGHTS 3)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100521e65l000j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
