\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Shirakawa: mkts still unstable over Greek debt\b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2010\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 21 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said on Friday financial markets remain unstable due to the Greek debt problem, and the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely watching current rapid moves in the markets.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general, including whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step into the market to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 He said he was keeping in close contact with his G7 counterparts on market developments.\par \par \uc2 After a policy meeting that ended earlier on Friday the BOJ outlined a loan scheme aimed at supporting growth industries and upgraded its assessment of the economy, and said Europe's debt situation needed watching for its impact on the global economy.\par \par \uc2 It left interest rates at 0.1 percent by a unanimous vote, as widely expected. (Reporting by Leika Kihara)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/SHIRAKAWA-MARKETS (URGENT)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|UKI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100521e65l000gg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
