\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2010\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN PARLIAMENT TO VOTE ON EURO RESCUE PLAN FRIDAY, OK EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's parliament is set to hold a key vote Friday on the country's contribution of up to EUR147.6 billion to a massive EUR750 billion bailout from European Union countries and the International Monetary Fund for euro-zone states on the verge of a default. (published 0708 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: GERMAN ECONOMIC ACTIVITY SLOWED IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Private sector activity grew more slowly in Germany during May, despite a sharp rise in export orders, according to a survey of purchasing managers. (published 0747 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN 1Q GDP +0.2% ON QTR, UNCHANGED FROM FLASH ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German economic activity expanded by 0.2% in the first quarter of this year from the last quarter of 2009 and rose 1.6% on the year, final federal statistics data confirmed Friday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK REAL-ESTATE LOANS IN DEFAULT SOAR BUT DEBT MARKETS REOPEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The amount of U.K. commercial property debt in default, or in breach of covenants, soared at the end of 2009, but that did not stop lenders from offering real-estate loans and opening the debt market again, a study by De Montfort University showed Friday. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB NOWOTNY: EURO-DOLLAR EXCHANGE RATE WITHIN HISTORICAL RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent weakening of the euro against the dollar hasn't reached a level where it causes concern at the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , governing council member Ewald Nowotny said in a guest column published Friday. (published 0732 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ REVEALS OUTLINE OF BANK LOAN HELP PLAN, UPS ECON VIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan policy board on Friday unveiled a broad outline of its bank lending support plan that includes offering loans to private banks for one year at a 0.1% interest rate, although the board put off a final vote on the matter. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: NEW LENDING STEPS NOT AIMED AT LOWERING RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's governor said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new measure to support bank lending to companies is not a step toward lowering interest rates. (published 0840 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SENATE PASSES WIDE-RANGING FINANCIAL OVERHAUL BILL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. senators passed an ambitious overhaul of U.S. financial markets on Thursday, channeling broad outrage at Wall Street into a measure that could force major changes at the nation's financial firms. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER HINT AT ACTION PUSHES YEN DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Friday hinted at possible government action to prevent any further rises in the yen, spooking investors into pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower in Asian trading. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WEST EUROPEAN SOVEREIGN CREDIT INDEX MOVES TIGHTER - MARKIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring debt issued by a collection of developed European sovereign borrowers moved lower early Friday, as a recovering euro led to a modest rally in credit markets. (published 0736 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIC EXECUTIVE: GREEK DEBT CRISIS UNLIKELY TO WORSEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's sovereign debt crisis is unlikely to worsen and the situation is showing signs of improvement, a senior executive with China's $300 billion sovereign-wealth fund said Friday. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN KAMEI: US, EU CAN GO AHEAD AND COMPLAIN TO WTO ABOUT JAPAN POST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's postal services minister Friday shrugged off pressure from the country's trading partners over attempts to reverse the privatization of its postal service, saying the U.S. and the EU should "go ahead" and file a complaint with the World Trade Organization. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US TREASURY: GEITHNER TO MEET UK, GERMAN OFFICIALS NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner will travel next week to the U.K. and Germany to meet with top economic officials and discuss ways to resolve the current economic crisis in Europe, the Treasury said Thursday. (published 2355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN FINANCE HEADS MULL TIGHTER FISCAL MONITORING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A European economic task force holds its first meeting Friday to beef up economic and budgetary surveillance in member states after the eurozone debt crisis that has roiled world markets. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH MIN: GROWTH MOMENTUM NOT DENTED BY DEFICIT CUT PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Growth recovery momentum in France won't be dented by the government's current plan to reduce the country's public deficit, French budget minister Francois Baroin said Friday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTER: EXPECT 'LESS ROSY' 2Q ECONOMIC DATA DUE TO UNREST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's finance minister said Friday that the country's economic performance is likely to be "less rosy" in the second quarter due to the impact of months of violent anti-government protests. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VENEZUELA'S CHAVEZ CALLS MOVE AGAINST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRADING 'WAR' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Hugo Chavez called his government's efforts to end unauthorized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading a "war" against rich Venezuelans in the financial world, and promised to raid more brokerage houses and imprison their directors. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BULL TREND TO CONTINUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Having set a record high at 128.58 Thursday, bunds will continue benefiting from the turmoil in global stock markets and look to extend the bull trend to meet projected resistance in the 128.80/90 area. A 1.618 upside extension target above there lies at 129.68. Completion of a bull pennant Thursday kept consolidation above 127.00, and corrective weakness should now be limited to the new range floor at 127.65. Longer-term bulls still have an eye on the psychological 130.00 target. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR EXTENDING GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Builds on the recovery off Wednesday's low at 1.2143, and the formation of a higher low at 1.2296 creates scope for further gains towards 1.2728. To force a break through there would tentatively leave 1.2143 as a near-term bear failure, and open the 1.618 upside extension target at 1.2773. The 1.2435 area has become intraday pivotal support, and a break below the 1.2296 higher low is required to bring the focus back onto the 1.2143. (published 067 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : YEN DOWN ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HINT, POLICY HOPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen fell against the euro and the dollar in Asia Friday after Japanese Finance Minister Naoto Kan said excessive strengthening of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't desirable, spooking market players who interpreted it as a hint that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market if the yen strengthens too much. (published 057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SENATE BILL: MANY POSSIBLE DINGS TO BANKS--AND A KEY FEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Landmark financial overhaul legislation passed by the Senate Thursday could put some dents in the earnings of the largest U.S. banks by changing some rules of investment banking, electronic payments including debit cards, and even the way banks manage risk in the mortgage business. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR SHOULD REBOUND ON FUNDAMENTALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wounds inflicted on the Australian dollar over the past 24 hours should heal soon, as buyers emerge who think the commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been pushed too low too fast, analysts say. (published 0440 GMT) [ 21-05-10 0801GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100521e65l000ix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
