\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says G7 won't discuss joint  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2010\par 04:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  finmin: G7 won't to discuss jointly supporting euro\par \par \uc2 * Kan: excessive, disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves undesirable\par \par \uc2 * Japan PM says "very worried" about market moves\par \par \uc2 * BOJ offers Y2 trln in market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soothe jitters (Adds analyst comments, details)\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - Group of Seven finance ministers are unlikely to discuss the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to support the euro in phone talks on Friday, Japan's finance minister said.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose against the dollar and the yen on Friday after a U.S. Treasury official said G7 finance ministers would discuss Greece's debt situation in a call the same day.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Naoto Kan, when asked about the Treasury official's comment, looked unsurprised but said Japan was unlikely to be asked to do much beyond expressing support for EU and IMF efforts to rescue Greece.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think this call is about joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I don't think the G7 is moving towards joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro," Kan said in a news conference.\par \par \uc2 "I don't want to speculate about what else will be discussed on the call. The EU and the IMF have agreed to help Greece. Japan will watch that process closely."\par \par \uc2 The euro tumbled to a 14-month low against the dollar and the yen surged on Thursday as fears of contagion stemming from the Greek debt crisis escalated and pushed U.S. stocks into negative territory for the year.\par \par \uc2 Despite Kan's comments ruling out joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , markets were on the lookout for any fresh message from the G7 on how it will deal with widening fallout from the Greek debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely, but the G7 could say they dislike volatile markets," said Shinichi Takasaka, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial products trading at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust & Banking Co in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "If the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't come up with appropriate measures, which I think it hasn't done so far, then the G7 might have to persuade the ECB to come up with something else. Markets are losing confidence."\par \par \uc2 JAPAN ALARMED\par \par \uc2 The yen's surge and sharp falls in Tokyo share prices have alarmed Japanese policymakers.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan offered 2 trillion yen ($22.03 billion) in funds to financial institutions in an emergency market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at soothing market jitters, the first time it has supplied liquidity on a same-day basis in about five months.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama said on Friday he was "very worried" about the market moves and said the government will act accordingly if needed, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 The government's chief cabinet spokesman also said he was closely watching the impact that a strong yen could have on Japan's still-fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 But Kan did not comment directly on whether Japan could step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem yen gains, only saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels should be determined by markets.\par \par \uc2 He also repeated that it was the shared understanding among G7 countries that excessive and disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were undesirable.\par \par \uc2 Kan said that while U.S. and Japanese share prices have fallen sharply, he expected market moves to stabilise over time with a framework for rescuing Greece now in place.\par \par \uc2 The IMF board is to meet on Sunday in Washington to act on its part of an aid package for Greece amounting to some 30 billion euros (around $40 billion), while the EU is to put up about 80 million euros of loans for Greece.\par \par \uc2 Greek lawmakers approved a 30 billion euro austerity bill on Thursday, paving the way for the record bailout from the EU and the IMF.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei average fell more than 4 percent to a two-month low on Friday, with exporters such as \uc2 Canon Inc\uc2  battered by worries that a stronger yen would curb their profits when repatriated.\par \par \uc2 A strong yen hurts Japan's export-reliant economy as it hurts the competitive advantage of Japanese goods overseas. ($1=90.77 Yen) (Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100507e65700065\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
