ional market gains post European settlement). Cable doing exactly the same, now a net 20 pips lower from the close of the polls and almost a whole point below the exit poll highs," says Penn. The issue is while the Conservatives are making gains against Labour, as expected, they are not making big enough gains against the LibDems, he says. A hung parliament, with the Conservatives as the largest party is the firm favorite result. June gilts stands at 117.82, and cable at $1.4849. (peter.nurse@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0210 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold's 2.8% ascent yesterday to beyond $1,200 shows strength of bull market, with NY close of $1,208.80 near session high of $1,212.60 positive as gold held on to gains even after losses in stocks pared, says Phillip Futures; adds gold proving "a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  alternative as investors lose faith in fiat \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." However, some profit taking in gold today; "our near term support level for gold is at $1,200. Should this level be breached, we will see a slight pullback and consolidation in prices before the upward trend continues." Spot gold at $1,201.10/oz, down $7.70. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0208 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP higher on risk aversion ahead of Monday's general polls while escalating worries over euro-zone debt crisis prompt safe-haven (USD) buying. Pair hits 2-month high at 45.78 vs 45.38 late Thursday. Still, upside likely limited for now as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of selling to support PHP, traders say. "The central was there at the opening, first at PHP45.50, then PHP45.60, offers were also made at PHP45.78," says local bank trader. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold around $50-$100 million, traders say. Resistance eyed at 45.90, next support 45.50. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com) [ 05-06-10 2239ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM0