\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-ANALYSIS-Puzzled by BOJ policy moves? Watch the yen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,086 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 03:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * BOJ policy moves may be guided by yen\par \par \uc2 * Further BOJ money market pumping seen having limited impact\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders may test Japan's ability to fight stronger yen (Repeats item that first ran on Thursday)\par \par \uc2 By Satomi Noguchi\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 11 (Reuters) - Trying to guess when the Bank of Japan will make its next policy move? For now, try watching the yen.\par \par \uc2 BOJ sources, talking to media including Reuters, have said in the past week that the board is considering expanding special money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just as the yen strengthened towards a 14-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 It is probably no coincidence that the yen was headed in exactly the same direction when the BOJ called an emergency meeting in December and pumped funds into the banking system in a move that changed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's course.\par \par \uc2 No one in the BOJ or the government, which is pressing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do more to fight deflation, has made an explicit link between the policy moves and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Instead officials talk of the need to fight deflation.\par \par \uc2 Any acknowledgment of the link might draw the BOJ and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which controls yen policy, into a battle with the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, requiring them to unleash the ultimate weapon in Tokyo's arsenal -- \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  deflation: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/xyb73j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/xyb73j }}}\uc2  More stories on Japan's economy: [ID:nECONJP] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 "The market would likely try to test the will of policymakers if the BOJ admits it is deciding monetary easing steps in relation to the yen's move up," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "I think BOJ officials know well the danger associated with such an official acknowledgement," said Sasaki, who used to work for an office in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the BOJ.\par \par \uc2 Apart from throwing down the gauntlet to hedge funds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, it would also be diplomatically untenable for Japan at a time when the old industrial powers of the G7 are trying to press China to ease its grip on the yuan.\par \par \uc2 It would be wrong though to accuse \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  of conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the back door.\par \par \uc2 IMPOTENCE\par \par \uc2 Sasaki likens the BOJ's policy moves to taking a toy gun into a standoff -- the ruse only works if the opponent believes it's real. In many ways the approach says much about impotence of the Japanese policymakers to stem the country's economic decline.\par \par \uc2 Burdened by debt approaching 200 percent of gross domestic product, the government can hardly go on a borrowing spree to pump-prime the economy.\par \par \uc2 With interest rates at 0.1 percent, there's little the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do either. The current crop of BOJ policymakers have little faith in quantitative easing, an experimental policy adopted after a 1990s property market crash that barely succeeded in pulling the economy out of deflation.\par \par \uc2 That leaves the yen.\par \par \uc2 A strong yen deepens deflation, already the worst on record in a country where prices have been mostly falling for more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 It also hurts exporters, undermining both Japan's terms of trade and corporate capital investment, the main drivers of economic growth before the global financial crisis triggered the country's worst ever recession in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan certainly had its eye on the yen when it called the December emergency meeting as government appeals for a policy response to deflation reached a crescendo.\par \par \uc2 At the meeting the BOJ decided to pump 10 trillion yen ($110.9 billion) in three-month funds into the banking system, helping push yen LIBOR rate below dollar LIBOR.\par \par \uc2 That nudged the yen lower against the dollar by making the yen relatively more attractive for funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  carry trades.\par \par \uc2 EFFECTS ON \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 After the emergency meeting, Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said that while the BOJ did not target the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in in setting policy, it was aware that news of the move would "have certain effects on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the long run".\par \par \uc2 The BOJ has also talked of the need to keep funding costs low for corporates by lowering short-term rates. Bank lending fell in February for a third month as smaller businesses refrain from borrowing, raising questions about how effective the policy might be in spurring economic activity.\par \par \uc2 Still, the BOJ appears to be considering increasing the size of the funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  or extending the three-month maturity to six months or longer.\par \par \uc2 While the BOJ and the government have not cited the yen as a concern this time, clouds are gathering in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Speculative traders in IMM futures boosted their long yen positions to 35,552 last week -- approaching the two-year peak of 51,710 reached last November as the yen hit 14-year high and just before the BOJ acted.\par \par \uc2 The yen surged to 84.82 yen to the dollar <JPY=> in late November, the highest since the record peak hit in 1995.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed as high as 88.14 yen last week. A day later Japan's Nikkei business newspaper reported that the BOJ was considering boosting its money supply \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There are other signs that the yen is moving up the list of policy priorities.\par \par \uc2 Last week the government lifted the amount of funds it can borrow to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nTOE62306R]\par \par \uc2 The 5 trillion yen increase gives it a war chest of 35 trillion yen ($390 billion) in case it needs to overtly stem yen strength by buying dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- something it has not done in six years.\par \par \uc2 It may have to resort to that option as the BOJ loses room for manoeuvre.\par \par \uc2 The absolute difference in rates is minuscule -- three-month yen LIBOR <JPYLIBOR> is now 0.249 percent and less than a basis point below comparable dollar LIBOR <USDLIBOR>. It was 4 basis points above dollar LIBOR in late November.\par \par \uc2 A further drop in short-term rates would take them near zero and could distort the money market in much the same way quantitative easing did between 2001 and 2006.\par \par \uc2 "These measures would probably exert only a limited and temporary impact on yen appreciation," said Seiji Shiraishi, Japan chief economist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Tokyo. (Editing by Eric Burroughs)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN (ANALYSIS, REPEAT)|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|NAT|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|UKI|G  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100312e63c00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
