\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Stars may realign for yen selling  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2    -- Neal Kimberley is an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are his own \par \par \uc2  By Neal Kimberley\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - While the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2004, the need to be seen to combat deflation could trigger a re-think in the new Japanese financial year beginning in April.\par \par \uc2  Of course the idea is an absolute outlier and to date there has been no hint that any such course is being contemplated.\par \par \uc2  But in any battle against deflation, unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an effective policy tool since it expands the supply of money. The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) has justified its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nGEE5B81FC] by explicitly presenting its efforts to curb Swiss franc gains as a complement to easy monetary policy.\par \par \uc2  The SNB's explanation of its policy has re-established a clear linkage between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy objectives that could be conscripted to justify any future Japanese action.\par \par \uc2  On the issue of monetary policy, it is noticeable that the domestic political emphasis on combating Japan's deflation has been growing in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Naoto Kan said on Tuesday he hoped the BOJ would take appropriate steps to pull the country out of deflation and that he wants prices to rise above zero, if not more, in 2010. [ID:nTKX006681]\par \par \uc2  By Friday, Kan was saying the Bank of Japan may be considering more easing measures after the government had requested additional efforts [ID:nTKF106878]. Sources familiar with the BOJ's thinking ventured that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would indeed this month debate a further easing of its already ultra-loose monetary policy. [ID:nTOE6230A7]\par \par \uc2  If such policy measures prove insufficient, it is possible that the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be seen as the weapon of last resort.\par \par \uc2  While many would scoff at such an idea given the six-year gap since the BOJ was last active, the Japanese government itself has sent a signal that could at least be interpreted as a greater readiness for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday raised its borrowing limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years. Under its fiscal 2010/11 draft budget, Japan will raise the borrowing ceiling for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  special account, the war chest it uses for yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by 5 trillion yen ($55.5 billion) to 145 trillion yen. [ID:nTOE62302G]\par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to authorize \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese government would certainly give advance warning to the United States.\par \par \uc2  In the recent past the U.S. administration would likely have opposed a policy that would artificially support or inflate the value of the dollar against the yen <JPY=>.\par \par \uc2  But circumstances may be changing.\par \par \uc2  Recent purported Chinese disinvestment from U.S. assets meant that in the December U.S. Treasury Department international capital (TIC) data, Japan was the biggest holder of U.S. assets with $768.8 billion. [ID:nN16219791]\par \par \uc2  Japan's position as a key ally of the U.S. is re-emphasized.\par \par \uc2  At the same time, there is a chance that a foreign policy issue which has clouded Japan-U.S. relations might finally be being addressed.\par \par \uc2  During his successful 2009 election campaign Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama raised the hopes of many in Okinawa that the U.S. Marines' Futenma airbase could be moved off the island.\par \par \uc2  Washington wants to stick to a 2006 deal to shift the facility to a less crowded spot on northern Okinawa.\par \par \uc2  On Friday a party elder of Hatoyama's ruling Democratic Party of Japan, Kozo Watanabe, argued that the Prime Minister may have to resign if the Okinawa issue is not resolved before the end of May. [ID:nTOE62407R] Watanabe believes that with a self-imposed deadline the premier could solve the problem.\par \par \uc2  If a face-saving solution to this issue can be brokered, the United States might look more benignly on any future Tokyo request regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  linked to the battle against Japanese deflation.\par \par \uc2  With EUR/JPY <EURJPY=R> hovering just above 120 yen, a long way below the 170 yen highs of July 2008, European objections would probably be muted.\par \par \uc2  Seoul could scarcely interject given that the Bank of Korea is already said to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the appreciation of the won <KRW=KFTC> against the dollar. [ID:nTOE62405W] \par \par \uc2  As Japan struggles with resurgent deflation [ID:nTOE61O06H] all policy tools need to be considered. In the new Japanese financial year this might ultimately include \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The idea should not be dismissed out of hand.\par \par \uc2  Biography of author [ID:nL9197090] \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-DOLLAR (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  COLUMN)|LANGEN|ABN|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100311e638000ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
